From: Project Luma
Subject: [PATCH] luma: AirPlay picker and unchosen network outputs in Sound Output

The Sound Output detail in Quick Settings gains an "AirPlay Speakers" row.
Expanding it asks luma-audio-devices (org.projectluma.AudioDevices1, package
luma-audio-policy) to look for receivers, and collapsing it, closing the
detail or closing Quick Settings stops the search. Choosing a receiver
connects it without closing the picker; a receiver with a password opens a
dialog modelled on the Wi-Fi password dialog, and other failures stay on the
row ("Owner Only", "Not Responding"). Remembered AirPlay outputs are listed
with the network speaker icon; outputs created by PipeWire's own discovery
modules (raop_sink., tunnel., rtp_session., snapcast) and any the service
reports in HiddenOutputs are left out unless one is the current output.
Without the service, the row is hidden and the menu behaves as before.

Rebased onto the series through 0118 (release .81); the stylesheet rules land after the Quick Options detail rules, ahead of the notification rules added by 0116.
